(2) The powers are the following -

(a) to extend the time within which notice of appeal may be

(b) to allow an appellant to be present at any proceedings;

(c) to order a witness to attend for examination;

(d) to admit an appellant to bail;

(e) to make orders under sections 42 l(2) and 4381(2) and to discharge or vary such orders; 0 to give directions under sections 436(1) and 438S(1); B.L.R.O. 10/2021 230 CAP.7 Criminal Procedure Code (& to make order under section 438 for the payment of

